"answer": "Project Zenith has received executive budget approval of $2M, though it was later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses to cover scope including real-time analytics. The project team was expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, ahead-of-schedule testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics during Phase Two. The project is currently in the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, with upcoming activities including a staff meeting on November 20th to discuss the analytics report, user interface enhancements planned for October, and new security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective next January. Additionally, partnership discussions with TechInnovate for AI technology are in early stages."
